diff --git a/roadmap/rendering.md b/roadmap/rendering.md
--- a/roadmap/rendering.md
+++ b/roadmap/rendering.md
@@ -4,6 +4,14 @@
 
 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-25 (2): look polish, lighter: fewer per-pixel and per-frame costs, same switches (type-checked NOWHERE: no Rust toolchain in the session, nothing compiled, run or validated with naga / glslang; the costs below are counted from the code, not measured; +1 test `look::the_face_boost_is_all_or_nothing`, `halos_are_capped_and_fade` tightened; run `cargo test --lib look pipeline` first, the shader tests validate the WGSL and every GLSL define).
+    - Far terrain: `flat_shade` (per PIXEL on the LoD, the largest area of the screen) took `pow(S, 1 + warm.w)` for each of its three face shades, two SFU ops a pixel for a constant. The three boosted constants are baked (`look::boosted`, `@SXB@` / `@SZB@` / `@SBB@` in both renderers) and `boosted()` picks one with `warm.w > 0`. Exact because `Look::new` writes `FACE_BOOST` or 0 and nothing between (the new test pins it). The vertex path (`chunk_shade`, a `pow` per vertex) is unchanged.
+    - Water: the sun glint did four `sin` / `cos`, two `normalize` and a `pow` for every top pixel of every water surface, in the sun or not. The half vector is now tested first: the ripples tilt the normal by at most 0.1 per axis, so a half vector with `y <= 0.85` cannot reach 0.93, and 0.93^160 is under 1e-5; those pixels (nearly all) skip the rest. Same picture. The depth gradient is untouched.
+    - Leaf sway: two trig calls a vertex instead of three (the y sway is a quarter of the difference of the x and z ones: still a smooth function of the position, so corners stay joined; amplitude at most 0.5 of `fx.z` as before).
+    - The block scan: `find_blocks` walks 32768 cells every frame and searched the six ids for each one; now one table read (`[bool; 256]`). `halos` selects the nearest `MAX_GLOW` with `select_nth_unstable_by` instead of sorting every emitter in reach (the blend is additive, the order is free).
+    - Caps lowered (the one visible change): halos 36 -> 16 at most and fading out between 16 and 28 blocks (was 24 and 40), motes 10 / 24 -> 6 / 14, sprite buffers 80 -> 40 quads (16 + the sun's + 14 + spare). A halo is a quad up to 3.4 blocks wide blended over the frame, so these are the fill-rate levers on a phone; the grade and every switch are as they were.
+    - Not changed on purpose: the final pass's grade (one `if` and about 25 ALU at surface size; 0 on the dial skips it), `finish()` (a smoothstep and two mixes a pixel, cheaper than a varying more), the light rays (7 thin triangles, only at a low sun), the sun's halo (one quad, only with the sun in view). Levers if a device still says no: `GRADE_*`, Motion Off, Water Look Off, `MAX_GLOW`.
+    - ponytail: weak GPUs (`present::weak_gpu`) get the same defaults as the rest; an Auto that starts them at Motion Low / Water Look off needs the GPU name before `Settings` is read (`App::init` loads `Settings` first). UNVERIFIED on a device: all of it; look at the lava lakes and a torch-lit cave for halos that now end sooner, and at the water's glint at a low sun against the previous build.
 - 2026-10-25: look polish: one Vibrance dial and five switches (type-checked on a Linux host and the shaders validated, not run on a device: all the numbers are taste values, judged by eye only; +8 tests in `render::look`, +1 in `options` and `world::atmos`, the `render::sky` fan test extended).
     - Where: `render/look.rs` computes one `Look` per frame (`Look::new(cfg, env)`), carried by `WorldDraw::look`; both renderers write the same numbers (the final pass's grade, the chunk block `U`: `warm`, `cool`, `sun`, `fx`, 176 bytes). `Look::OFF` is the identity in every shader.
     - 1 Grade: `grade()` in the final pass (`present.rs`, and the GLES `present` source), in sqrt space, skipped when the dial is 0. Vibrance lifts what is dull (`1 + v * (1 - saturation)`) and leaves vivid greens and blues alone; S-curve `mix(g, g*g*(3-2g), k)`; warm highlights / cool shadows `+-k` on red / blue by luma. The dial scales all three: at 1.0 vibrance +0.5, curve 0.35, split 0.05; default 0.3 (+0.15 / 0.105 / 0.015). Costs one `if` and a few ALU in the pass that already runs, in Fast and Full alike.
